From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:17:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] foundry, lsp: look up programs off the main thread

A file's first diagnostics pass, and each language server's start when a
pipeline finishes loading, looked up the program on the main thread: in
the pipeline's runtime with ide_pipeline_contains_program_in_path(), then
on the host. Each lookup spawns `which` and waits for it, and in a podman
runtime that is a `podman exec`, 134-177 ms each. With a toolbox as the
runtime, opening a Python file froze the editor for 0.3-0.8 s: flake8 for
the diagnostics, then ruff and pylsp when the pipeline loaded.

_ide_pipeline_find_programs_async() makes the same lookups on a worker
thread, filling the runtimes' path caches. Both are IdePathCache, which
locks, and the podman runtime starts its container under a mutex.
IdeDiagnosticTool runs it before each pass, and IdeLspService once per
pipeline before it creates the launcher. Both then make their lookups on
the main thread as before, and find every answer cached. The SDK
extensions of a Flatpak configuration are left to the main thread, as
before.
